    "             - If we want to claim such like \"$H_a$: CV of malfunctioning detector data is over 0.2\", we need to use the sample of the malfunctioning data.\n",
    "            - Therefore, left-tailed test (less than) is more supported as the sample mean of the CV is expected to be less than the hypothesized value (upper threshold).\n",
